          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life and Military Service</strong><br>\nMuammar Gaddafi was born in a Bedouin tent near Sirte, Libya, on June 7, 1942. From humble beginnings, he rose through the military ranks after completing his education at the Libyan Military Academy and in the United Kingdom.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Revolution and Seizure of Power</strong><br>\nIn 1969, Gaddafi led a bloodless coup that overthrew King Idris of Libya. He was 27 years old at the time and quickly established himself as the de facto leader of the country, promoting a philosophy drawn from Arab nationalism, socialism, and Islam.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Ideological Foundations and \"The Green Book\"</strong><br>\nGaddafi developed his political and social philosophy, outlining it in \"The Green Book.\" His ideology rejected both communism and capitalism and proposed a system he called \"Islamic socialism,\" which aimed to distribute wealth evenly among the populace.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
