          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Reign and Revolutionary Committees</strong><br>\nThroughout his rule, Gaddafi used revolutionary committees to control the population. He also funded various liberation movements worldwide while maintaining an iron grip on Libya's wealth, generated primarily through its oil reserves.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Foreign Relations and Sponsorship of Terrorism</strong><br>\nGaddafi's foreign policy was marked by a series of confrontations with the West. Libya was implicated in several international terrorist incidents, leading to UN sanctions and strained international relations.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Pan-Africanism and African Union</strong><br>\nGaddafi was a strong proponent of Pan-Africanism, advocating for a united Africa. He played a crucial role in the formation of the African Union, aiming to create a single currency and united military force for the continent.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
