            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Domestic Policy and the \"Jamahiriya\" System</strong><br>\nGaddafi introduced the \"Jamahiriya,\" or \"state of the masses,\" in Libya, which he claimed was a form of direct democracy, though in practice it was considered authoritarian, with power concentrated in his hands.</p>\n\n<p><strong>c1</strong><br>\nEarly Life of </p>\n\n<p><strong>Trygve Lie was born in Oslo, Norway, in 1896. He grew up in a time when Norway was undergoing significant changes, becoming an independent nation in 1905. Lie was educated as a lawyer and quickly became involved in Norwegian politics, joining the Labour Party and serving in various governmental positions.</strong><br>\nEntry into Politics</p>\n"
              },
